From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp1: give the PinePhone Pro sensors a usable colour
 pipeline

The rkisp1 tuning files for the PinePhone Pro sensors were added in 2023 by
commit 36435e2ae ("ipa: rkisp1: Add tuning files for PinephonePro sensors")
and have only ever carried lens shading tables:

    ov8858: Agc, Awb, LensShadingCorrection
    imx258: Agc, Awb, BlackLevelCorrection, LensShadingCorrection

libcamera's own generator, utils/tuning/rkisp1.py, emits a much longer list for
any rkisp1 sensor, including several StaticModule entries that take fixed
parameters rather than measured data and so need no calibration:

    tuner.add([agc, awb, blc, ccm, color_processing, filter,
               gamma_out, lsc, lux, wdr, compress])
    gamma_out = StaticModule('GammaOutCorrection', {'gamma': 2.2})

Enable those here. GammaOutCorrection matters most: with no output gamma the
ISP hands out near-linear data and the preview is dark and flat. Measured on a
PinePhone Pro front sensor, same white wall before and after:

    before:  black floor  66   median  85   p99 105   range 33
    after:   black floor 143   median 179   p99 201   range 45

Also add colour correction matrices. No rkisp1 tuning file upstream contains a
CCM - not one of the seven - so camera RGB reaches the display uncorrected and
saturated colours come out muted and hue-shifted; a bright red renders as a
dark orange. Proper matrices require a Macbeth chart, which does not exist for
these sensors, so the ones here are borrowed from the closest same-vendor
sensors that libcamera does ship measured data for: ov5647 (Raspberry Pi VC4
tuning) for the ov8858, and imx219 for the imx258. A CCM corrects colour
mixing, which is broadly similar across comparable colour filter arrays, so a
same-vendor matrix is a large improvement over the identity matrix that applies
today. It is explicitly an approximation, not a calibration: expect red to read
as red rather than orange, but not colorimetric accuracy.

Measured chroma energy on one scene: 3.18 with nothing, 9.75 with the CCM.

ColorProcessing is enabled with saturation left at 1.0. Raising it to 1.5 was
tried and reverted: a CCM already supplies saturation, so the two compound and
a white wall picks up visible pink and green casts (chroma energy 16.68).

Two things are deliberately NOT done here. WideDynamicRange and Compress made
no measurable difference to brightness or range while slightly increasing
chroma error. And the AWB is left as grey world: switching to the bayes
algorithm needs a 'colourGains' curve, and unlike a CCM that curve encodes the
sensor's absolute per-channel response - what white actually looks like on that
silicon. Borrowing ov5647's produced a grossly wrong white point (mean V 65.6
against a neutral 128, i.e. a solid green cast), so it must be measured rather
than transplanted.

While here, give the ov8858 camera sensor helper its black level, the same way
commit 27e4d3fc3 did for the imx258. Without it the IPA logs on every open:

    WARN RkISP1Blc blc.cpp:72 No black levels provided by camera sensor helper,
                              please fix

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN fin_a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp fin_b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -758,6 +758,8 @@
 public:
 	CameraSensorHelperOv8858()
 	{
+		/* From datasheet: 0x40 at 10bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
 		/*
 		 * \todo Validate the selected 1/128 step value as it differs
 		 * from what the sensor manual describes.
diff -ruN fin_a/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/imx258.yaml fin_b/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/imx258.yaml
--- a/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/imx258.yaml
+++ b/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/imx258.yaml
@@ -5,6 +5,25 @@
 algorithms:
   - Agc:
   - Awb:
+  - Ccm:
+      ccms:
+        - ct: 2860
+          ccm: [ 2.121, -0.525, -0.596, -0.853, 2.804, -0.951, -0.269, -1.148, 2.417 ]
+        - ct: 2960
+          ccm: [ 2.270, -0.542, -0.728, -0.770, 2.603, -0.833, -0.260, -1.513, 2.773 ]
+        - ct: 3603
+          ccm: [ 2.186, -0.661, -0.525, -0.778, 2.695, -0.916, -0.252, -0.831, 2.083 ]
+        - ct: 4650
+          ccm: [ 2.182, -0.709, -0.473, -0.702, 2.764, -1.062, -0.252, -0.720, 1.971 ]
+        - ct: 5858
+          ccm: [ 2.324, -0.884, -0.440, -0.638, 2.583, -0.945, -0.285, -0.541, 1.827 ]
+        - ct: 7580
+          ccm: [ 2.212, -0.532, -0.679, -0.579, 3.079, -1.500, -0.277, -0.733, 2.010 ]
+  - ColorProcessing:
+      saturation: 1.0
+  - Filter:
+  - GammaOutCorrection:
+      gamma: 2.2
   - BlackLevelCorrection:
   - LensShadingCorrection:
       x-size: [ 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625 ]
diff -ruN fin_a/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/ov8858.yaml fin_b/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/ov8858.yaml
--- a/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/ov8858.yaml
+++ b/src/ipa/rkisp1/data/ov8858.yaml
@@ -5,6 +5,26 @@
 algorithms:
   - Agc:
   - Awb:
+  - BlackLevelCorrection:
+  - Ccm:
+      ccms:
+        - ct: 2873
+          ccm: [ 1.882, -0.262, -0.619, -0.638, 2.115, -0.477, -0.135, -0.997, 2.133 ]
+        - ct: 2965
+          ccm: [ 2.150, -0.519, -0.632, -0.536, 1.926, -0.390, 0.018, -1.486, 2.467 ]
+        - ct: 3606
+          ccm: [ 1.975, -0.438, -0.537, -0.562, 1.998, -0.436, -0.124, -0.771, 1.895 ]
+        - ct: 4700
+          ccm: [ 2.010, -0.515, -0.495, -0.521, 2.010, -0.489, -0.095, -0.673, 1.768 ]
+        - ct: 5890
+          ccm: [ 2.136, -0.653, -0.483, -0.484, 1.931, -0.448, -0.135, -0.548, 1.683 ]
+        - ct: 7600
+          ccm: [ 2.066, -0.392, -0.674, -0.509, 2.275, -0.766, -0.140, -0.661, 1.801 ]
+  - ColorProcessing:
+      saturation: 1.0
+  - Filter:
+  - GammaOutCorrection:
+      gamma: 2.2
   - LensShadingCorrection:
       x-size: [ 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625 ]
       y-size: [ 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625, 0.0625 ]
